course: dictionary
lesson: 9775
title: Who is a surgeon?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A surgeon is a doctor who does operations. An operation means cutting into the body to repair or remove a part that is hurt or unwell. «A surgeon is a doctor who operates on the body.» When you meet the word surgeon, think: a doctor trained to do operations.
explain: Surgeon is a noun, so it names a person. You can have one surgeon or many surgeons. Look at the words around it for clues. «Put under» means a deep, safe sleep so nothing hurts, so a surgeon works while the patient is asleep.
explain: Surgeons are not the only people who cut and care for living things. A tree surgeon cuts and looks after trees. Read the words before and after to check which kind of surgeon is meant.
fact: A surgeon is a doctor who does operations.
fact: A tree surgeon is a person who cuts and looks after trees.
fact: Surgeons wash their hands carefully and use clean tools to stop germs.
fact: In robotic surgery, the surgeon sits at a console and controls the robot arms.
fact: In the UK, surgeons are called «Mr» or «Ms», not «Dr».
exercise: «A surgeon is a doctor who operates on the body.» What is a surgeon? | A teacher of science | *A doctor who does operations | A person who sells plants | A nurse who gives out medicine
exercise: «In robotic surgery the surgeon sits at a console and controls the robot arms.» Who is in charge of the robot arms? | The patient | *The surgeon | The robot itself | A computer alone
exercise: Mia says a tree surgeon is a doctor for people. What is a tree surgeon really? | *A person who cuts and looks after trees | A robot that climbs trees | A doctor who does operations on people | A type of tree
test: Why do surgeons use clean tools and wash their hands carefully? | To make the operation longer | *To stop germs | To keep the room cold | To look smart
test: Which word means a doctor who does operations? | Patient | *Surgeon | Console | Germ
exam: «A surgical robot moves only when the surgeon moves its controls.» What does this tell us? | The surgeon is not needed | Robots can work alone at night | *The surgeon stays in charge of the robot | The robot decides what to do
